       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. A single 5000 mg dose is also well above the usual 1,000 mg maximum per dose. That amount could cause serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth three times daily (about 2 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day), which is within the 4 g/day limit\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 5000 mg really is what you intend, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd still advise checking with pharmacy first."
